Z||000005||Oreif||03-22-2001||06:39 PM||||I get that from some idiots at work sometimes. Of course once they actually see the car they can't believe it's a Fiero. The best part is they drive cars that are big POS's. On guy use to make fun of Fiero's. Then one day he asked for some help getting his car started, It was a Ford Festiva with over 200,000 miles on it. 0 compression. We could push the car even with the cutch engaged. He doesn't say anything about Fiero's anymore. Cost him over $1500 to fix the car. (Cracked head) I think that is twice what it was worth! <P>Don't worry about what other people say. Besides if he even knew anything about the car he'd want one too.||||reg||1
